WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- We have reached the end of the hour,

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:04.050
but I have one more story
from social media to share.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:05.160
This is #What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.710
(rhythmic jingle)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.630
We've shared a lot of love this hour,

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:10.620
and to close the show,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:12.840
I'd like to share some
love for our sponsor.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.780
As many of you know, Pilot
G2 pen is the go-to pen

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.832
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:00:16.832 --> 00:00:19.500
I love it, but I'm not alone, y'all.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.620
Chris Grosse, an assistant
athletic director at Penn State,

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:26.077
recently post this to his
11,000 Twitter followers.

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:27.870
"You can only write with one type

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.150
of pen for the rest of your life.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.920
Which one are you picking?"

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.170
The post had over 50,000,000 views,

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.050
and of course the G2 pen
blew away the competition

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:37.943
'cause this is how they do it.

00:00:37.943 --> 00:00:38.776
(crowd applauding and cheering)

00:00:38.776 --> 00:00:39.750
Let's get Chris in here.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.150
He's watching on ABC23.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.219
What's up Chris?

00:00:43.219 --> 00:00:44.730
(crowd cheering)

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:45.563
- How's it going, Kelly?

00:00:45.563 --> 00:00:46.680
Thanks for having me.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.090
- Okay, I wanna get this outta the way

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:50.550
so nobody thinks this: you're
not being paid by them.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.350
This is just what happened, right?

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.560
- No, I was actually working from home

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.360
here in central Pennsylvania.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.470
There was a snowstorm,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.200
and I was down in our basement working

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.810
at my wife's work from home desk,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:07.290
and noticed she had an
amazing collection of pens,

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:10.770
and included in that was
my personal favorite,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.120
the Pilot G2 pen,

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.640
and you know, I love how it writes,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.640
I love the grip, and I love
that you can just click it

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.460
to, you know, pass the time
when you're in long meetings,

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.040
and, you know, I wondered
if there were other people

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.920
that had strong pen opinions like I did,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.710
and so I laid out a
whole bunch on the floor

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.690
and snapped a photo and tweeted it out,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.670
and the rest is history.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:33.570
- Oh man, it's so fun.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:35.010
Thank you so much, Chris.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:35.880
This is super fun.
(audience applauding)

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:37.422
I'm liking your post right now,

00:01:37.422 --> 00:01:38.255
(heart dings)

00:01:38.255 --> 00:01:39.088
and that's not all.
- Thank you so much.

00:01:39.088 --> 00:01:41.280
- Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.020
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.570
want to show you as much
love on this Valentine's Day

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.390
as you've shown them, so, get this,

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.460
they are hooking you up
with a lifetime supply

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.579
of G2 pens and a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.161
(audience applauding and cheering)

00:01:54.161 --> 00:01:55.288
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:55.288 --> 00:01:57.503
A lifetime supply. Unbelievable.

00:01:57.503 --> 00:01:58.740
- [Kelly] Look at the power

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:00.330
of one tweet, Chris.
- Oh, that's great.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.163
- That was awesome.

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:01.996
Thank you, Chris,

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:03.390
and thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.940
Ashton Kutcher, Chrissy
Metz, Bradley Collins,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.860
Summer, Lee, and Mckai, oh Mckai.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:10.530
Happy Valentine's Day, y'all.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.090
Remember, love us all around us.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.440
We just have to let it in.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.550
Have a great day, and if it's not,

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:15.843
well, try and change it.

